  23:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****   ==============================================================================
  24:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****                     ##### IWDG Generic features #####
  25:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****   ==============================================================================
  26:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****   [..]
  27:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****     (+) The IWDG can be started by either software or hardware (configurable
  28:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****         through option byte).
  29:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c **** 
  30:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****     (+) The IWDG is clocked by the Low-Speed Internal clock (LSI) and thus stays
  31:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****         active even if the main clock fails.
  32:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c **** 
  33:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****     (+) Once the IWDG is started, the LSI is forced ON and both cannot be
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccqzT16d.s 			page 2


  34:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****         disabled. The counter starts counting down from the reset value (0xFFF).
  35:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****         When it reaches the end of count value (0x000) a reset signal is
  36:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****         generated (IWDG reset).
  37:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c **** 
  38:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****     (+) Whenever the key value 0x0000 AAAA is written in the IWDG_KR register,
  39:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****         the IWDG_RLR value is reloaded into the counter and the watchdog reset
  40:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****         is prevented.
  41:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c **** 
  42:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****     (+) The IWDG is implemented in the VDD voltage domain that is still functional
  43:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****         in STOP and STANDBY mode (IWDG reset can wake up the CPU from STANDBY).
  44:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****         IWDGRST flag in RCC_CSR register can be used to inform when an IWDG
  45:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****         reset occurs.
  46:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c **** 
  47:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****     (+) Debug mode: When the microcontroller enters debug mode (core halted),
  48:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****         the IWDG counter either continues to work normally or stops, depending
  49:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****         on DBG_IWDG_STOP configuration bit in DBG module, accessible through
  50:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****         __HAL_DBGMCU_FREEZE_IWDG() and __HAL_DBGMCU_UNFREEZE_IWDG() macros.
  51:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c **** 
  52:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****     [..] Min-max timeout value @32KHz (LSI): ~125us / ~32.7s
  53:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****          The IWDG timeout may vary due to LSI clock frequency dispersion.
  54:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****          STM32G0xx devices provide the capability to measure the LSI clock
  55:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****          frequency (LSI clock is internally connected to TIM16 CH1 input capture).
  56:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****          The measured value can be used to have an IWDG timeout with an
  57:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****          acceptable accuracy.
  58:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c **** 
  59:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****     [..] Default timeout value (necessary for IWDG_SR status register update):
  60:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****          Constant LSI_VALUE is defined based on the nominal LSI clock frequency.
  61:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****          This frequency being subject to variations as mentioned above, the
  62:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****          default timeout value (defined through constant HAL_IWDG_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT
  63:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****          below) may become too short or too long.
  64:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****          In such cases, this default timeout value can be tuned by redefining
  65:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****          the constant LSI_VALUE at user-application level (based, for instance,
  66:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****          on the measured LSI clock frequency as explained above).
  67:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c **** 
  68:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****                      ##### How to use this driver #####
  69:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****   ==============================================================================
  70:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****   [..]
  71:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****     (#) Use IWDG using HAL_IWDG_Init() function to :
  72:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****       (++) Enable instance by writing Start keyword in IWDG_KEY register. LSI
  73:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****            clock is forced ON and IWDG counter starts counting down.
  74:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****       (++) Enable write access to configuration registers:
  75:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****           IWDG_PR, IWDG_RLR and IWDG_WINR.
  76:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****       (++) Configure the IWDG prescaler and counter reload value. This reload
  77:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****            value will be loaded in the IWDG counter each time the watchdog is
  78:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****            reloaded, then the IWDG will start counting down from this value.
  79:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****       (++) Depending on window parameter:
  80:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****         (+++) If Window Init parameter is same as Window register value,
  81:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****              nothing more is done but reload counter value in order to exit
  82:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****              function with exact time base.
  83:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****         (+++) Else modify Window register. This will automatically reload
  84:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****              watchdog counter.
  85:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****       (++) Wait for status flags to be reset.
  86:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c **** 
  87:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****     (#) Then the application program must refresh the IWDG counter at regular
  88:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****         intervals during normal operation to prevent an MCU reset, using
  89:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c ****         HAL_IWDG_Refresh() function.
  90:Drivers/STM32G0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g0xx_hal_iwdg.c **** 
